<body class="article">
<div id="header">
<h1>Extensions API</h1>
</div>
<div id="content">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>One of the major improvements to Asciidoctor recently is the extensions API.
AsciidoctorJ brings this extension API to the JVM environment allowing us to write extensions in Java instead of Ruby.</p>
</div>
<div class="admonitionblock note">
<table>
<tr>
<td class="icon">
<div class="title">Note</div>
</td>
<td class="content">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>If you are migrating existing extensions to a newer version, please see the guides:</p>
</div>
<div class="ulist">
<ul>
<li>
<p><a href="guides:extension-migration-guide-16-to-20.html">guides:extension-migration-guide-16-to-20.html</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><a href="guides:extension-migration-guide-15-to-16.html">guides:extension-migration-guide-15-to-16.html</a></p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Writing an extension is as simple as creating a Java class and sub-classing from one of the extension points.
However, to explore the full potential it&#8217;s recommended to:</p>
</div>
<div class="olist arabic">
<ol class="arabic">
<li>
<p>Have a brief understanding of the AsciidoctorJ conversion process and internal representation of the document.
In short, extensions allow you to tap into the conversion process to make modifications to enhance the generated content.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Write an extension class.
This is as simple as creating a subclass from one of the extension points listed below.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Register your class to make AsciidoctorJ converter aware of it.
There several options depending on the use case.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Asciidoctor provides eight types of extension points.
Each extension point has an abstract class in Java that maps to the extension API in Ruby.</p>
</div>
<table class="tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch">
<caption class="title">Table 1. AsciidoctorJ extension APIs</caption>
<colgroup>
<col width="20%">
<col width="40%">
<col width="40%">
</colgroup>
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">Name</th>
<th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">Class</th>
<th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="include-processor.html">include-processor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.IncludeProcessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Intercepts <code>include::[]</code> lines</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="preprocessor.html">preprocessor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.Preprocessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Allows you to modify the asciidoc text before parsing</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="block-macro-processor.html">block-macro-processor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.BlockMacroProcessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Processes block macros like <code>bibliography::[]</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="block-processor.html">block-processor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.BlockProcessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><div class="content"><div class="paragraph">
<p>Processes an arbitrary block based on it&#8217;s style such as</p>
</div>
<div class="literalblock">
<div class="content">
<pre>[prohibited]
--
Do not enter
--</pre>
</div>
</div></div></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="treeprocessor.html">treeprocessor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.Treeprocessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Modify the AST after parsing.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="inline-macro-processor.html">inline-macro-processor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.InlineMacroProcessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Processes inline macros like <code>btn:[]</code>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="postprocessor.html">postprocessor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.Postprocessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Modifies the backend-specific output document.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code><a href="docinfo-processor.html">docinfo-processor.html</a></code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><code>org.asciidoctor.extension.DocinfoProcessor</code></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Insert content into the <code>header</code> element or the end of the body element (html), or the <code>info</code> element or at the end of the document (docbook).</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
